  "term": "hyperkinetic syndrome",
  "definition": "Hyperkinetic syndrome is a childhood-onset behavior disorder marked by levels of inattention, impulsivity, and hyperactivity that are not appropriate for the person’s developmental stage. Both inattention and hyperactive-impulsive symptoms are often present, though one pattern may be more prominent than the other.",
